 damping.\n\n- $y'' +4y'+3y = 0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping" 13194139534688 17592186045417 false] [17592186147373 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $y'' +y'+2 y = 0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping.\n\nII. $y'' +2y'+ y = 0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n\nIII. $y'' +4y'+3y = 0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186147444 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432827 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186147445 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432828 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186147446 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432829 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186147447 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432826 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186147704 1050 600.0 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186148179 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n- ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+8y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping.\n- ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping." 13194139534688 17592186045417 false] [17592186148179 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n\nII. ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+8y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping.\n\nIII. ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping." 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186148180 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186148180 1071 "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with light damped harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+13y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the damped oscillation?" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186148180 1071 "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with light damped harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$y^{″} + 6y^{′} + 13y = 0$,\n\nwhere $t > 0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the damped oscillation?" 13194139534688 17592186045417 false] [17592186148180 1074 "The given equation represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. We are looking for solutions of the form $y={e}^{\\lambda t}.$\n\nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +13=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +13 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+13 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t).\n$$\n\nFrom the solution, the value of the angular frequency is $Ω=2\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.$\n\nThe period of the damped oscillation $T$ is related to the angular frequency as follows:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{Ω}\n$$\n\nSo the period is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{2}=\\pi \\,\\text{s}.\n$$" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186335726 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n- ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping.\n- ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping." 13194139534688 17592186045417 false] [17592186335726 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n\nII. ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping.\n\nIII. ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping." 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186357723 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping\n- ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping\n- ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical  damping" 13194139534688 17592186045417 false] [17592186357723 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping\n\nII. ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping\n\nIII. ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical  damping" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186357725 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${y}^{″}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping\n- ${y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+9y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping\n- ${y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+14y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping" 13194139534688 17592186045417 false] [17592186357725 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}^{″}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping\n\nII. ${y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+9y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping\n\nIII. ${y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+14y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432797 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432797 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432797 1083 #uuid "01d92886-a0b6-558c-8d1d-01e1a39fc792" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432798 1080 "2\\pi \\,\\text{s}" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432798 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432798 1083 #uuid "12588678-dc2f-56ca-b7ad-d201ff8cd771" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432799 1080 "{y}^{″}+9y={e}^{t}" 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432799 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534688 17592186045417 true] [17592186432799 1083 #uuid "23192ffb-